  <section class="page-header">
    <h1>Living in Andorra</h1>
    <p>
      A small sovereign country in the Pyrenees. The working week is the
      test, not a Saturday on the slopes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Scale</h2>
    <p>
      Andorra is a co-principality between France and Spain. You can drive
      the main valley in well under an hour. A working capital, ski
      parishes and high villages share one set of institutions.
    </p>
    <p>
      It is not a suburb of Barcelona or Toulouse. Catalan is the official
      language. Spanish and French are widely used. English is common in
      professional rooms and less so in the village shop. Current
      Government notes expect new residents to move towards Catalan at
      renewal. Confirm the level then required on
      <a href="https://www.govern.ad/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
        >Govern.ad</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>A year in the mountains</h2>
    <p>
      Winter is the public season: Grandvalira on the eastern side,
      Pal-Arinsal and Arcalís in the west. The slopes sit next to the
      villages. That is why it feels different from a long-transfer Alpine
      resort.
    </p>
    <p>
      Summer is quieter and, for many people who stay, better. High
      trails, the Madriu-Perafita-Claror landscape, Sorteny and
      Comapedrosa are the outdoor map. Autumn is short and clear. Spring
      is the melt.
    </p>

    <h2>Where to live</h2>
    <p>
      The seven parishes are the real map. Andorra la Vella and
      Escaldes-Engordany hold most appointments and the public hospital.
      Ordino and Canillo are higher. La Massana and Encamp sit on ski
      roads. Sant Julià de Lòria is the southern gate, closer to Spain and
      the university.
    </p>
    <p>
      Read the
      <a href="/parishes">parish notes</a>
      before you ask an agent to search. Housing that works for a
      residence file is not the same as a holiday chalet. See
      <a href="/properties">properties</a>
      for how we will list homes, and
      <a href="/directory">the directory</a>
      for AGIA-registered agents.
    </p>

    <h2>Schools and health</h2>
    <p>
      Education is plural. Govern.ad publishes three systems: Andorran,
      Spanish and French. Non-Andorran schools also teach Formació
      Andorrana, so Catalan and Andorran institutions are on the
      timetable. The public university sits in Sant Julià de Lòria. The
      official links are on
      <a href="/education">education</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Public healthcare is organised by
      <a href="https://saas.ad/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SAAS</a>,
      which describes Hospital Nostra Senyora de Meritxell as the
      country’s only hospital and runs primary-care centres in the
      parishes. Social security is
      <a href="https://www.cass.ad/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CASS</a>.
      Coverage depends on affiliation. Read
      <a href="/healthcare">healthcare</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Money and paper</h2>
    <p>
      Daily banking is local. The Association of Andorran Banks lists
      three groups:
      <a href="/directory/andbank">Andbank</a>,
      <a href="/directory/morabanc">MoraBanc</a>
      and
      <a href="/directory/creand">Creand</a>.
      Opening an account is a compliance meeting, not a form. The
      supervisor is the
      <a href="https://www.afa.ad/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">AFA</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Driving-licence photographs and signatures are taken at Government
      premises, by appointment, on the
      <a
        href="https://www.e-tramits.ad/tramits/renovacio-del-permis-de-conduir/p/GV000303"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">official e-tramits pages</a
      >. Border conditions under the European Entry/Exit System are on
      <a href="/practitioner-map">the practitioner map</a>,
      using the Govern.ad dates.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you are moving, start with
      <a href="/become-a-resident">become a resident</a>
      and the official immigration pages:
      <a href="/residence-without-work">D.1</a>,
      <a href="/family-reunification">B.1</a>,
      <a href="/tax-residence">tax residence</a>.
      The registers themselves are on
      <a href="/official-sources">official sources</a>.
      For an introduction, use the form on the residency page or write to
      <a href="mailto:hello@privateandorra.com">hello@privateandorra.com</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
